WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.872
There are two common ways to retrieve dictionary values.

00:00:03.872 --> 00:00:08.032
Square brackets work when you are confident the key exists.

00:00:08.032 --> 00:00:13.337
Ticket priority is safe because priority is present in the record.

00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:16.522
Get is useful when a key may be missing.

00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:25.353
Owner does not exist, so ticket dot get returns the default value “unassigned” instead of raising an error.

00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:32.025
This is especially helpful with real-world records where some fields may be optional or incomplete.
